SDL3_net AmigaOS 68k notes
=============================

Build:
  make -f Makefile.amiga

Individual CRT variants:
  make -f Makefile.amiga clib2
  make -f Makefile.amiga libnix

Outputs:
  build/clib2/lib/libSDL3_net.a
  build/libnix/lib/libSDL3_net_libnix.a

SDL3 linkage:
  clib2  -> -lSDL3
  libnix -> -lSDL3_libnix

AmigaOS socket backend:
- Opens bsdsocket.library v4 in NET_Init().
- Closes bsdsocket.library in the final matching NET_Quit().
- Includes proto/bsdsocket.h and proto/exec.h.
- Uses CloseSocket() instead of close().
- Uses IoctlSocket(FIONBIO) instead of fcntl(O_NONBLOCK).
- Emulates the poll() functionality needed by SDL3_net through WaitSelect().
- Uses Errno() for bsdsocket.library socket errors.
- Hostname resolution is synchronous on classic AmigaOS because SocketBase
  is task-local and must not be shared with SDL resolver worker tasks.

The upstream local-interface enumeration has no classic AmigaOS backend in
this port yet, so NET_GetLocalAddresses() may not enumerate interfaces.
Core client/server, stream/datagram and hostname resolution paths are the
focus of this first port.
